---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config/site';
import { FEE_DATA_VERSION, FEE_DATA_UPDATED } from '@/data/fees';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology & Editorial Policy"
  description="How FeeCalc Tools sources, verifies, and updates payment processor and creator fee schedules — correction log and changelog included."
  canonicalPath="/methodology/"
  modified={FEE_DATA_UPDATED}
>
  <h1>Methodology & editorial policy</h1>
  <p class="answer-first">
    I store every fee schedule in one versioned data file with a source URL and last-verified date. Calculators use a
    transparent percent-plus-fixed formula with a documented reverse equation. Current data version:{' '}
    {FEE_DATA_VERSION} (updated {FEE_DATA_UPDATED}).
  </p>

  <h2>How calculations work</h2>
  <p>
    Forward: <code>fee = charge × percent + fixed</code>, <code>net = charge − fee</code>. Reverse:{' '}
    <code>charge = (desiredNet + fixed) ÷ (1 − percent)</code>, rounded to cents. Unit tests cover every schedule.
  </p>

  <h2>Sourcing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Prefer the provider’s official pricing or fee policy page.</li>
    <li>Record currency, percent, fixed fee, and notes for regional caveats.</li>
    <li>When processing varies (Patreon, Ko-fi), label figures as blended estimates.</li>
    <li>
      On each tool, rates are phrased like RealFeeCalc: “Checked &lt;date&gt; on &lt;provider&gt; pricing page.”
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What the calculators leave out</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Custom negotiated rates, volume discounts, and unpublished enterprise pricing.</li>
    <li>Chargeback fees, monthly software fees, and hardware costs unless noted.</li>
    <li>Sales tax, VAT, and income tax.</li>
    <li>FX spreads beyond the published conversion add-ons we model as percent schedules.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="ai">AI / automation disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    Drafts may be written with AI assistance; every formula, rate and reference is checked by {siteConfig.authorName}{' '}
    against the sources listed on each page.
  </p>

  <h2>Update cadence</h2>
  <p>
    Fees change often. When a published rate changes, I update <code>src/data/fees.ts</code>, refresh last-verified
    dates, bump <code>FEE_DATA_VERSION</code> / <code>FEE_DATA_UPDATED</code> when material, run{' '}
    <code>npm test</code>, and only then change on-page “Last reviewed” dates. Dates do not change for cosmetic edits
    alone.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the official pricing URL for the schedule.</li>
    <li>Update percent, fixed, currency, notes, sourceUrl, lastVerified.</li>
    <li>Bump version fields when material.</li>
    <li>Run tests and build.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="changelog">Changelog</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <time datetime="2026-10-20">2026-10-20</time> — Mobile SEO audit fixes; named maintainer (Hammad Iqbal); TrustBlock
      sources; favicon/manifest set; Consent Mode GA4; guide slug fixes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <time datetime="2026-10-19">2026-10-19</time> — Initial public fee data version {FEE_DATA_VERSION} published.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="corrections">Correction log</h2>
  <p>Confirmed mistakes and fixes. Empty means none reported yet since launch.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <time datetime="2026-10-20">2026-10-20</time> — Removed anonymous “Team” authorship that could not be supported
      (same honesty fix RealFeeCalc documented). Replaced with named maintainer {siteConfig.authorName}.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> with evidence. I prioritize
    corrections that include an official URL.
  </p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>No payment brand sponsors default rankings. Comparison sorts are by calculated fee for the selected amount.</p>
</BaseLayout>
